    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10061" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condylus</span></b>  (‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condŭlus</span></b> , Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
			38, 14</span></i> Müll.), i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόνδυλος</span>. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The knob</i> or <i>knuckle of a
			joint;</i> esp. <i>plur., the fist</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">complicatis in condylos digitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 88</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> (<i>A joint of a reed;</i> hence meton.)
				<i>A reed</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 5,
				78, 30</span></i> dub.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> = anulus, Paul. ex Fest. l.
		l.</div>
